sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor Dev as Developer
  participant CLI as shelf-bench CLI
  participant CB as Cloud Build + Artifact Registry
  participant CR as Cloud Run job
  participant T as Task (runner.py)
  participant BILL as Billing Catalog API
  participant GCS as Cloud Storage
  participant GEM as Vertex AI Gemini
  participant RET as Embeddings + AlloyDB (optional)

  Dev->>CLI: make cloud (shelf-bench cloud-run -a ... -m ...)
  CLI->>GCS: upload source tarball
  CLI->>CB: create build
  CB-->>CLI: image pushed (poll until SUCCESS)
  CLI->>CR: create / patch job (image, args, one task per approach x tier x model)
  CLI->>CR: run execution
  par every task in parallel
    CR->>T: start task N (approach, model, tier)
    T->>BILL: fetch live prices (Gemini, embeddings, Cloud Run, GCS, USD to INR)
    T->>GCS: read annotations + seeded sample of test images
    loop each image (4 workers)
      T->>GEM: generateContent (single_pass: 1 call / detect_classify: detect then classify)
      GEM-->>T: boxes + labels, usage_metadata (tokens, traffic type)
      opt retrieval approach (its own embedder, DB and SQL)
        T->>RET: embed crop (utils/embeddings), then its SQL query (utils/alloydb)
        RET-->>T: closest products (vector or hybrid)
      end
      Note over T: score vs ground truth (IoU >= 0.5), cost from token buckets + ctx.bill units
    end
    T->>GCS: write images.jsonl + summary.json (provisional compute cost)
  end
  CLI->>CR: poll execution until all tasks finish
  CLI->>GCS: pull new runs into results/
  CLI->>CR: Admin API: task start / completion times
  CLI->>GCS: write summary with final compute cost
  Dev->>CLI: make ui
  CLI-->>Dev: leaderboard + step-by-step run pages
